      "writtenOn": "2017-08-11T16:12:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is quite interesting, so more spreading instead of packing is giving benefits in your experiment due to the frequencies increase with more packing (I mentioned the freq changes within the lower end of the spectrum compared to the higher end, since the same capacity increase at the higher end would have higher energy cost).\n\nThis is not quite generic, I think that lower cap_idx may not mean lower power consumption since we may be comparing values from different clusters.  Energy delta would be sorted out by the energy diff on whatever target_cpu we choose anyhow, but we are just increasing the chances of picking an idle cpu here",
